# Force LF everywhere, whatever the checkout platform's own autocrlf setting is. Several tests slice
# source files by literal string search (e.g. "\n}\n" to find a function's closing brace) and only
# match LF - a Windows checkout with core.autocrlf=true silently converts every file to CRLF on disk,
# which breaks those tests locally even though the actual committed content (and Vercel, and CI) is
# pure LF and correct. This makes every checkout match what is actually committed.
* text=auto eol=lf
